** Project 01 - Aerospace Mounting Bracket
** STANDALONE TEST: linear static analysis on structured hex mesh
** Scope: verification plate only (see chat log) - NOT the general
** bracket meshing strategy.
**
** All physics identical to the tet-mesh verified case:
**   Geometry: 60x40x4 mm plate, x=cantilever length, y=width, z=thickness
**   Material: Al 7075-T6, E=71700 MPa, nu=0.33
**   BC: root (x=0) fully fixed (encastre)
**   Load: 235.44 N transverse force at tip free-edge centroid via
**         reference node + DISTRIBUTING coupling to tip facial surface
**   Targets: sigma_max=132.4 MPa, delta_tip=1.108 mm (Euler-Bernoulli)
**
** NOTE: reference node ID must exceed the mesh's real max node ID
** (confirmed 88386 for this mesh) to avoid silently overwriting a
** real mesh node - see chat log, this was the actual cause of the
** first hex-mesh solve failure, not a mesh-quality problem.

*INCLUDE, INPUT=mesh_hex_clean.inp
*INCLUDE, INPUT=nsets_hex.inp
*INCLUDE, INPUT=tip_facial_surface_hex.inp

*NODE
200000, 60.0, 20.0, 2.0
*NSET, NSET=REF_TIP
200000

*MATERIAL, NAME=AL7075T6
*ELASTIC
71700., 0.33

*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=plate, MATERIAL=AL7075T6

*BOUNDARY
root, 1, 3

*COUPLING, REF NODE=200000, SURFACE=TIP_FACE, CONSTRAINT NAME=TIP_COUPLING
*DISTRIBUTING
1,3

*STEP
*STATIC

*CLOAD
200000, 3, -235.44

*NODE FILE
U
*EL FILE
S
*END STEP
